{"name":"Garbanzo Paste","hex":"#eec684","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"garbanzo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible pulse (Cicer arietinum), of the family Leguminosae or Fabaceae and subfamilies Faboideae or Papilionoideae, with white or purple-blue flowers and small feathery leaves on both sides of the stem and pods containing two to three peas.","A seed of this plant; the chickpea."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garbanzo"},{"term":"paste","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft moist mixture, in particular:\nOne of flour, fat, or similar ingredients used in making pastry.\n Pastry.\n\nOne of pounded foods, such as fish paste, liver paste, or tomato paste.\nOne used as an adhesive, especially for putting up wallpapers, etc.","One of flour, fat, or similar ingredients used in making pastry."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To stick with paste; to cause to adhere by or as if by paste.","To insert a piece of media (e.g. text, picture, audio, video) previously copied or cut from somewhere else."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paste"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chickpea","blocks":[{"text":"The chickpea or chick pea is an annual legume of the family Fabaceae, subfamily Faboideae, cultivated for its edible seeds. Its different types are variously known as gram, Bengal gram, chana (চানা), garbanzo, garbanzo bean, or Egyptian pea. It is one of the earliest cultivated legumes, the oldest archaeological evidence of which was found in Syria."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Chickpea_BNC.jpg/330px-Chickpea_BNC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chickpea","wikidata":"Q81375"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Cicer_arietinum_noir_MHNT.BOT.2017.12.2.jpg/500px-Cicer_arietinum_noir_MHNT.BOT.2017.12.2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut